  "description": "Sweet kiwi is accented with the slightly licoricey flavor of tarragon in this easy gin cocktail.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Garnish: tarragon sprig\n\nNotes: To make simple syrup, combine 1 cup water with 1 cup sugar in a small saucepan and heat over medium heat, stirring constantly, until sugar is dissolved. Cool before using. Simple syrup will keep in a sealed container in the refrigerator for up to 5 days. If your kiwi is super-sweet, you might not need the full half ounce called for here.",
